        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="0" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="1" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test shows a very high level of air leakage in this house. This sitaution lead to an increase of the energy required and the cost to heat the interior space. We recommend to increase the level of air tightness of the house by installing weather strips on the windows and doors. We notice a hole behind the microwave that lead to the chimney of the previous heating system. This hole must me closed and selaed to prevent air leakage and animals to enter inside the house.

</airSeal>
                <foundation>The foundation walls are not insulated at the exception of one room. We estimate the insulation to be R-12. We recommend to add R-20 to reach a level of R-30. Concerning the uninsulated section we recommend the installation of R-30. 



Be cacreful with the insulation, place the vapour barrier or material that are also vapour barrier on the warm side of the wall. Make sure that the joints are well sealed.



When you insulate an exterior wall, the exterior face become colder than before and therefore any leaks of the humidity inside the building that cross through the insulation could turn in condensation and lead to formation of mould.</foundation>
                <windows>We notice that some windows leaks. This situation is more important on the windows on the upper floor. We recommend the replacement of the windows by new windows. If your planning the replacement you must look for the followings specifications to choose the units that fits the best the northern climate.



- ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED

- TRIPLE GLASS

- INSULATED 

- ARGON

- LOE-E COAT



The replacement of windows can help to increase the air tightness of your home.  </windows>
                <AdditionalComments>During the inspection of the attic we notice some black marks on the inside part of the sheating that seems to be mould. At the moment of the inspection it seems to be a result of a previous problem that happen before. At the moment of the inspection we haven't notice any activities. We recommend to monitor this situation by verifying the attic. The next time could be after the heating season. If the sitation is wrost than before it means that there is some heat passing from the interior space to the roof without going through the insulation.

If you notice the creation of ice on this particular section or anywhere else, it's an indicator of air leakage on the roof.



Incresing the air tightness of tne house will arise the level of humidity of the house. In that case the situation can change if the problem still present and also make it wrost.



For the moment your first step is just to observe and monitor the situation, in this way it will help you to be in control of the situation.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
